  "note": "Annual election of one third (five seats). Only five candidates were nominated; when the time for withdrawals expired on Monday 7 January the town clerk, J. W. Pollock, declared them elected for three years. Mahaffy, Malcolm and Uprichard were retiring members; G. A. Anderson and J. V. Malcomson did not seek re-election. The Irish Weekly, 12 January 1929, p. 11 (\"No Contest in Lurgan\"), reports the same five."
